From 73ee883f89ca7aec6e39012d27308a44d0096ee8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:26:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] worker-placement: a not_claimable reserve lost to
 the reserved worker's claim is a pickup, not a refusal

Probe t_01a19fd990770095 (hub, 11-03): the Board reserved the card for worker-1, worker-1 claimed it at
05:21:51Z, and the hub's next reserve from a copy without that lease got 409 not_claimable at 05:21:52Z.
worker-placement recorded board_refused and commented "Board placement request refused" although the card
ran fine on worker-1 (the local `claimed` event arrived after the refusal was written).

On not_claimable, when the latest queue observation is an assignment to machine X, pull the feed once and
treat a lease (or a Board `claimed` event newer than that observation) held by X as the pickup: no
board_refused reason, no refusal comment. No current reservation, a failed pull (any error; the
batch goes on), or a lease held by another machine keep the refusal, fenced on the row the Board refused (pre-pull)
so the queue guard does not silence it; every card in the tick is judged against the row and reservation its reserve
was made from (snapshotted before the loop). The extra pull runs at most once per tick. Also rewords the `mixed` code ("Candidates excluded for multiple reasons"), which was
untrue for one candidate carrying several reasons.

Card: t_01a19fdd27fcdcca
